{
  "summary": "Fixes migration of watch-only legacy wallets containing transactions in migratewallet. It makes database transaction listener callbacks optional to prevent unhandled std::bad_function_call exceptions when aborting transactions. Additionally, it adjusts the migration completeness check in CWallet::ApplyMigrationData to account for pending transaction deletions rather than checking in-memory state before commit.",
  "problem": "Users attempting to migrate legacy wallets that contain watch-only addresses and transaction history encounter a complete migration failure. The migration validation checks whether the in-memory wallet map is empty before transaction deletions are committed, which fails and triggers a database transaction abort; the abort then invokes an unset callback that throws std::bad_function_call and bypasses cleanup.",
  "evidence": [
